  "behavior": [
    "Private HashMap<usize,ListNodeOwner<T>> indexes original owned pointers and per-node allocators. Canonical BaseList links alone retain node order, iteration, and nonpanicking destruction order. Native value-node layout is unchanged.",
    "Current-node lookup uses only an opaque address as key and returns the original retained allocation pointer; it never fabricates pointer provenance from an address.",
    "Cursor value/change_value/next perform expected constant-time membership lookup. Removal uses the current head or a live remembered predecessor whose actual next link is current; stale predecessor state falls back to canonical chain scan.",
    "Safe cursor predecessor preservation, native canonical observer phases, callback-time Drop, allocator identity and public auto traits remain covered by original scoped regressions.",
    "Four additional deterministic regressions cover registry growth/splice/reversed destruction, repeated head removal, retained traversal/search miss, and repair after freed remembered predecessor. No timing thresholds are asserted."
  ],
